From: Darcy Phipps <dphipps@qnx.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Mar 2025 11:44:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/60] Get contrib/fribidi building on QNX

fribidi's meson build adds the -ansi flag to the build if it detects
that the compiler supports it. I'm not sure why.

QNX8 no longer supports this option. Normally meson's compiler feature
detection would pick up on this but because the meson build process
in the docker doesn't work with qcc/q++, I have to specify the
underlying compiler directly. That compiler _does_ support "-ansi" so it
gets turned on.

The build then fails when including stdlib.h because it makes use of
"inline" which "-ansi" does not allow.

Remove the usage of "-ansi" when QNX is in play.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific (from qnx-ports)

diff --git a/contrib/src/fribidi/0001-qnx-remove_ansi_compiler_flag.patch b/contrib/src/fribidi/0001-qnx-remove_ansi_compiler_flag.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..e05fbc09299
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/src/fribidi/0001-qnx-remove_ansi_compiler_flag.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+--- fribidi/meson.build
++++ fribidi/meson.build
+@@ -21,10 +21,6 @@ libversion = '@0@.@1@.0'.format(soversion, interface_version, interface_age)
+ # C compiler. This is the cross compiler if we're cross-compiling
+ cc = meson.get_compiler('c')
+ 
+-if cc.get_id() == 'gcc' and cc.has_argument('-ansi')
+-  add_project_arguments('-ansi', language: 'c')
+-endif
+-
+ # Symbol visibility
+ have_visibility_hidden = false
+ if host_machine.system() != 'windows'
diff --git a/contrib/src/fribidi/rules.mak b/contrib/src/fribidi/rules.mak
index 881b3c2aa47..2d32f0a612d 100644
--- a/contrib/src/fribidi/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/fribidi/rules.mak
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@ $(TARBALLS)/fribidi-$(FRIBIDI_VERSION).tar.xz:
 
 fribidi: fribidi-$(FRIBIDI_VERSION).tar.xz .sum-fribidi
 	$(UNPACK)
+ifdef HAVE_QNX
+	$(APPLY) ${SRC}/fribidi/0001-qnx-remove_ansi_compiler_flag.patch
+endif
 	$(MOVE)
 
 # FIXME: DEPS_fribidi = iconv $(DEPS_iconv)

